# lf159, the slow physician of the hill (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle lf159
revision 1
state ready
dialect larkfield
accent none
tier standard
written_for rm_egil_grantham
written_by claude
title the slow physician of the hill
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=healer talk=quiet
traits temper=calm talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk trusts_no_remedy_mixed_in_a_house_still
likes pickled_herring singing old_maps frosty_mornings
dislikes stale_bread smoke
fears a_fever_that_will_not_break smoke_settling_on_the_hill
hopes a_winter_with_no_fevers in_good_voice_at_the_midwinter_singing
topics health +0.5 work +0.4 weather +0.3 pastimes +0.3 dreams +0.2 gossip -0.5
styles comfort=patient gossip=closed refuse=soft tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# climbs the hill each day with a physician's bag: quiet, unhurried and a little dreamy, mixing every remedy by hand and trusting none that came out of a House's still-room.

words
oath! = Clean paws and patience | By the cool basin
saying! = Rest does what physic can't | Slow is a remedy too | Sit with it before you treat it
bag = my bag | the old leather bag
rounds = my rounds | the rounds up the hill
remedy = a remedy | a remedy I mixed myself
basin = the basin | a basin of cool water
herring = pickled herring | a herring, sharp with vinegar
whitefrost = a white frost | frost on the railings
song = a song | a song in good company
chart = an old chart | a chart drawn mostly by guesswork
stairs = the long stairs | the stairs up the hill
lowsmoke = the smoke | coal smoke off the low streets
hardcrust = a hard crust | bread gone to stone
stillroom = some House's still-room | a still-room with a crest on the door
pulse = the pulse | a slow, steady pulse
hill = the hill | the hill above the city
calls = my calls | the calls on the hill
patient = a patient | the one I'm sitting with
fever = a fever | a fever that won't break
cough = a cough | a cough that rattles
sickroom = a sick room | the room with the curtains drawn
window = a window | the window nearest the bed
sleep = sleep | a long night's sleep
downs = the downs | the open downs
sick = the sick | the sick on the hill

any
opinion @1 houses for 1 : The Houses keep #hill# in order. I'd not take a drop of their physic, but I'll grant them that. | I go into House doors every week. I mix my own #remedy# before I go.
opinion @1 drink against 1 : I've bound up enough heads after a feast to have no love for #drink#. | One cup with #supper# does no harm. More than that is a visit from me, often as not.
opinion @1 city against 1 [self.away=yes] : The city crowds #sick# into rooms with no window. In #self.from_town# you could at least open a door onto #downs#. | Too many chimneys. I'd move every one of them further from #stairs# if I could.
opinion @1 sump against 1 : I've not gone below the Commons on #rounds#. I'm told I'd be needed there more. That sits poorly with me. | I don't know the Sump. That's the truth, and I'm not proud of it.
opinion @1 times for 1 : I'll not complain of the times. #hill.capitalize# pays its physician, and pays on the day. | The times are kind to me. I try to be kind back, to #sick# especially.
opinion @1 watch for 1 : With the Watch about, the street is quiet at night, and a quiet street sleeps better. #sleep.capitalize# mends more than I do. | A constable has sent for me more than once, to #sick# in the street. I think well of them for it.

grown
line @1 greet [pair.band=strangers] : #greet#. You've the look of someone who walked up the hill. Sit a moment. | #greet#. Take your breath first; there's no hurry.
line @2 greet [self.working=yes self.job=healer] : #greet#. I'm on #rounds#, but I can stop a minute. | #greet#. Forgive the smell of #basin#; it's only vinegar.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Good morning. #hill.capitalize#'s quiet yet; I like it so. | Good morning. Up early. So am I, most days, on #rounds#.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : Good evening. You're abroad late on #hill#. | Good evening. I've only just put #bag# down.
line @1 again.open : #welcome_back#. You look well, at least. | Twice today. That pleases me.
line @1 greet.return : #greet#. | #greet#. It's good to see you.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : #greet#. Come and sit. | #greet#. You were in my head on #stairs# just now.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes self.job=healer] : #greet#. Walk with me; I've a call to make. | #greet#. Quietly, please. Somebody's sleeping in there.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Go gently.
line @2 farewell [here.time=dusk|night] : Good night. Keep warm going down #stairs#. | Good night. #sleep.capitalize# is the best of medicine.
line @1 farewell.return : #farewell#. | #farewell#. Take care on #stairs#.
line @1 react.news : Is it. Tell me slowly; I'd like to understand it. | Go on. #listen#.
line @1 react.news.new : #surprise#. Nobody on #hill# has said so. | That hasn't reached #rounds# yet.
line @1 react.news.known : #knew#. A patient told me this morning. | I'd heard. They talk to the physician as if I were a wall.
line @1 react.news.doubt : #doubt#. I'll wait for someone who saw it with their own eyes. | Perhaps. I've heard a great many things on #stairs# that were never so.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : I'm sorry. #pity#. | That is hard. Sit with it a while; there's no hurry.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : #gladnews#. I'm very glad. | That's #good#. That's very good to hear.
line @1 answer.how : #fine#. Nobody worse today than yesterday. | Well enough, thank you. Slow, as ever. #bc_always_is#
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : #busy.capitalize#. There's a cough going round the hill. | Many #calls# today. I'll take them in turn, slowly.
line @1 ask.how : And you? Are you getting #sleep#? | How are you keeping? Truly, now. #howso#.
line @1 sympathise : #sympathy#. Sit; give it a moment. | That's a weight. You needn't carry it standing.
line @1 reassure : #reassure#. It mends slower than you'd like, but it mends. | Give it time. #saying#.
line @1 decline : #hedge#: I can't come today. I've a fever on the hill that I'll not leave. | I'm sorry, I must say no. #rounds.capitalize# won't wait, and nor will the sick.
line @1 accept_decline : #no_matter.capitalize#. Another time. | It's no matter. I understand, truly.
line @1 thank : #thanks#. That was kind. | Thank you. I'll keep that in mind a long while.
line @1 deflect_thanks : #deflect.capitalize#. It's what I do. | It was nothing. #sleep.capitalize#, and we're square.
line @1 preclose [self.working=yes] : Well. #rounds.capitalize# are waiting. | I should be getting on. Someone's expecting #bag#.
line @2 preclose : Well. #preclose#. | I'll let you go. #excuse#.
line @1 accept_preclose : Of course. Go gently, #address#. | Go on, then. #farewell#.
line @1 ack : #bc_true# | #bc_i_know#
line @1 give.advice : #advise.capitalize#: sleep, and drink water, and wait. Most things pass. | Open #window#. Smoke does more harm than half what I'm called for.
scene the_morning_rounds
when topic=work|day self.job=healer self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I've seven calls on #rounds# today. I'll see them all by dusk, slowly. | I climb #stairs# every morning with #bag#. My legs know every step. | I sit with each patient longer than they expect. Most of them only want listening to.
b : Seven? | Every step? | Only listening?
a : Seven. #cough.capitalize#, two fevers, a bad knee, and three who are lonely and call it something else. | Every one. There's a loose stone near the top of #stairs# I always step over. | Mostly. I listen first, and then I look at #pulse#. The listening tells me more.
b : #bc_wise# | #bc_ha# | #bc_true#

scene the_old_bag
when topic=work self.job=healer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #bag.capitalize# was second-hand when I bought it. It's had three owners and it's outlived two. | Everything in #bag# I mixed myself. Nothing in it came from a still-room. | I keep a clean cloth on top of #bag#. It's the first thing I reach for.
b : That's a long life for a bag. | Nothing at all? | A cloth?
a : Longer than I'll have, I expect. It will go to whoever comes next. | Nothing. #saying#. | To wash with, and to cover. A cloth does more good than most bottles in #stillroom#.

scene no_house_physic
when topic=health|work self.job=healer
does give.opinion / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I'll use nothing out of #stillroom#. I mix my own, every drop. | A House sent me a cordial for #patient# last month. I poured it out and made my own. | I trust #remedy#. I can't say what's in a House's bottle.
b : Why not? | Was that wise? | Do they put something in it?
a : Because I don't know who stood at the still, or what they wanted. A plain remedy wants no master. | It was mine to answer for. Their cordial wasn't. The patient mended. | Probably nothing. But I've no way to know, and that's enough.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_true# | #bc_wise#

scene sitting_with_a_fever
when topic=health|work self.job=healer self.working=yes
does tell.worry / reassure / assess / ack
a : There's a fever on #hill# that won't break. I sat up with it till the small hours. | I've #patient# I'm worried for. I'll go back after dark. | Some nights there's nothing to do but wait with #sick#. So I wait.
b : It'll break. | That's good of you. | That must be hard.
a : It will. I'll be by #window# when it does. | It's the job. The better part of it, I think. | It is. It's also the part that matters most.
b? : #bc_i_hope_so# | #bc_true# | #bc_true#

scene frosty_morning
when topic=weather|season here.season=winter here.time=dawn self.likes=frosty_mornings
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #whitefrost.capitalize# on everything. I stopped on #stairs# to look at it. | A frosty morning clears the head. I breathe deeper on #hill#. | #whitefrost.capitalize#, like salt. I wished I could keep it.
b : It's cold, though. | Deeper? | It'll be gone by noon.
a : Cold and clean. Better than warm and smoky, any day. | The air's thin and sharp. Every #cough# eases on a morning like this. | It will. That's part of why I like it.

scene smoke_from_below
when topic=weather|health here.region=ridgemere self.dislikes=smoke
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : #lowsmoke.capitalize# came up the hill this morning. Every chest I listened to rattled. | I can't abide smoke. Half of what I treat on #hill# starts with a chimney. | On a still day #lowsmoke# sits on the stairs like a lid.
b : It's the city. | Half? | I've seen it.
a : It is. That doesn't mean I have to like it. | Half, or near it. Open windows would put me out of #work#, and I'd thank them. | Then you've breathed it. Go up #hill# on a windy day, and breathe that instead.

scene rain_on_the_stairs
when topic=weather here.weather=rain here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Rain on the hill again. #stairs.capitalize# are running like a stream. | I carry #bag# under my coat in the rain. The coat gets wet; the bag doesn't. | Rain keeps #lowsmoke# down, at least. I'll forgive it that.
b : It never stops. | Sensible. | That's something.
a : It stops. Not often, and never for long. | #bag.capitalize#'s older than the coat. It has seniority. | It is. There's always something, if you look slowly enough.

scene herring_supper
when topic=food self.likes=pickled_herring
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #herring.capitalize# and a piece of bread. That's supper, and I'll want nothing more. | There's always #herring# on my shelf. One fish at night, and I sleep well. | People wrinkle their noses at #herring#. More for me.
b : Just that? | Every night? | It's an acquired taste.
a : Just that. A plain #supper# sits well. | Most nights. I'm a creature of habit, slowly. #bc_every_night# | Acquired, and kept. I've had it a long time.

scene hard_crusts
when topic=food self.dislikes=stale_bread
does tell.complaint / react.complaint / assess
a : I was given #hardcrust# at a house today and ate it to be polite. My jaw still aches. | There's no excuse for #hardcrust#. Wrap the loaf. | I'd sooner go hungry than eat #hardcrust#. I'd sooner, and I have.
b : That's manners. | Easier said. | Have you?
a : Manners, and a sore tooth. I'd not do it twice. | It's easier done than chewing it, I'd say. | Once or twice, on a long day. I didn't mind the hunger as much.

scene singing_in_company
when topic=pastimes|friends self.likes=singing
does invite / accept_invite / assess / ack
a : There's #song# at a friend's house tonight. Come along, if you like. Nobody minds a poor voice. | I like #song# more than almost anything. I don't speak much, but I'll sing. | Some evenings we sing the old songs together. I know all the low parts of #song#.
b : I'd like that. | You sing? | The low parts?
a : Good. Bring nothing but yourself. | Badly, and gladly. It's the only time I'm loud. | Somebody has to hold the bottom. I'm steady, if nothing else.
b : #bc_good# | #bc_ha# | #bc_true#

scene old_charts
when topic=pastimes|travel self.likes=old_maps
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I collect #chart# when I can find one. The older the better. | I've #chart# that puts the city on the wrong side of the Sound. I love it more than the right ones. | I read old charts the way some read stories. Every one is somebody's idea of the world.
b : The wrong side? | Why old ones? | Somebody's idea?
a : The wrong side, and the Sound twice too wide. Someone guessed, and guessed bravely. | Because they're wrong in interesting ways. The new ones are only wrong in dull ones. | Somebody who never walked it. I like to think about what they hoped was there.

scene the_heights
when topic=home here.region=ridgemere self.quarter=heights
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The Heights are quiet. Nobody hurries up here; it suits a slow walker. | I live up the hill, near #stairs#. I can hear the bells but not much else. | Up here the sick are rich, but they're no less sick. #fever.capitalize# doesn't read a door knocker.
b : Peaceful. | Just the bells? | That's true.
a : It is. I wouldn't trade it, though I'm not sure I earned it. | The bells, and the rain, and #song# on a good night. | It's the first thing I learned on #hill#.

scene home_downs
when topic=memories|home self.away=yes self.from=larkfield
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : #self.from_town# was home. The weather showed itself over the downs an hour before it arrived. | Back in #self.from_town# there was no physician. My #gran# set bones on the kitchen table. | I think of #downs# on frosty mornings. The whole hill white, and the sheep steaming.
b[from=larkfield] #lark : An hour, and you'd still get wet. | Every family had one like that. | Steaming, yes. I'd forgotten.
b : Do you miss it? | On the table? | Steaming?
a@lark : We would. We'd watch it come anyway. | Most of what I know started with her. | I hadn't, quite. I'm glad to be reminded.
a : Some mornings. It was the sky over #downs#, mostly. Here there are roofs in the way. | On the table, with #song# to keep you still. It worked. | Their breath in the cold. It looked like a whole field breathing.

scene faith_quietly
when topic=faith
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : Before each call I ask the Bright One's help. I couldn't tell you whether it helps the patient. | Sermons pass me by. I sing at the feasts; that's my part of it. | When a fever breaks, I think the Bright One had a hand in it. When it doesn't, I think I didn't try hard enough.
b : It helps you, maybe. | That's enough. | That's a hard way to think.
a : Perhaps that's what it's for. #bc_maybe# | It's what I can give. | It is. I'd change it if I knew how.

scene the_long_dream
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail / assess
a : I dream sometimes of a winter with no fevers at all. I walk #rounds# and nobody needs me. | I dreamt I followed #chart# and the city really did sit across the Sound. | Last night I dreamt I was singing and couldn't stop. It was rather pleasant.
b : Would you like that? | Was it? | What were you singing?
a : I would. I'd walk #stairs# anyway, I think, just to be sure. | It was. It was a better city, too. Quieter. | An old harvest song. I've not sung it in years. I woke up humming.
b : #bc_lovely# | #bc_ha# | #bc_lovely#

scene keeping_quiet
when topic=gossip|crime|health
does tell.gossip / react.news / insist / ack
a : People tell the physician everything in #sickroom#. I tell no one anything. | Much is said to me on #rounds#. None of it leaves the room it was said in. | Someone asked me today what was wrong with a neighbour of theirs. I said I didn't know. I did.
b : Not even a hint? | Never? | That's discreet.
a : Not even that. A sick room is only safe if it's shut. | Never. That's the whole of the trade, nearly. | It's the only way they'll keep sending for me.
b : #bc_fair_enough# | #bc_true# | #bc_true#

scene lean_winter
when topic=times|health world.times=hard|lean
does tell.worry / reassure / assess
a : In lean times #cough# goes on longer. Hungry chests don't mend. | I've been taking bread on #rounds# as well as #remedy#. Bread does more. | There are more calls in a lean month. Fewer can pay. I go anyway.
b : That's hard. | That's good of you. | You go anyway?
a : It is. #saying#, but rest wants a full belly. | It's not good. It's only sense. | Anyway. A physician who only goes to those who pay isn't one.

scene a_trusted_friend
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : #self.friend# is someone I'd sit up with through any fever. | I've few friends; I don't talk enough for many. #self.friend# is one. | #self.friend# can tell when I want quiet. That's a rare kindness.
b : High praise, from you. | One's enough. | Rare, yes.
a : It's true, which is better. | One is plenty, so long as it's the true one. | Rare and worth more than it costs.

scene a_new_face
when topic=newcomer|player
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Someone new has come up #hill#. Tired from the road, by the look. I hope they've a bed. | Travellers bring coughs up #hill# with their luggage. I listen to them anyway. | A stranger wanted the chapel and didn't know the stairs. I walked them there; it was on #rounds#.
b : I hope so too. | Anyway? | Kind of you.
a : Most do, up here. I'll keep an eye out, quietly. | #cough.capitalize# doesn't care where it came from. Nor do I. | It lay along #rounds#. Everything does, if you walk slowly enough.

story the_first_patient [topic=work|memories self.job=healer self.age>=25]
  : The first patient I ever sat with alone was an old drover with a broken wrist. I was shaking more than he was.
  : He told me to sing something while I set it. So I did, badly.
  ask : Would you have laughed?
  b : I'd have tried not to.
  b[old] : I'd have sung along, I think.
  : He did laugh. And then it was set, and he said it didn't hurt as much. I've sung at every one since.

story the_frost_fair [topic=season|memories self.away=yes self.from=larkfield self.age>=20]
  : One winter in #self.from_town# the frost was so hard the river froze, and they held the market on the ice.
  : I was a #child#. I remember the stalls creaking and nobody minding.
  ask : Have you ever stood on a frozen river?
  b : Never. I'd be too frightened.
  b[from=larkfield] : I remember that winter. Or my family did.
  : It held. Everything holds, if it's cold enough. I've always liked a hard frost for it.

story the_herring_jar [topic=food|memories self.age>=20]
  : My #grandad# kept a jar of herring by his bed and swore it kept him young.
  : He lived to a great age. Whether it was the herring, I couldn't say.
  b : Maybe it was.
  : I keep a jar by mine. I've stopped asking it questions.

rule @rounds_bark
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=healer
does aside
cooldown 8h
say #calls.capitalize#: seven today. One at a time. | Mind the loose stone. Always the loose stone.

rule @smoke_bark
when concept=bark self.dislikes=smoke here.region=ridgemere
does aside
cooldown 10h
say #lowsmoke.capitalize# again. Open a window, someone. | That smoke will be #cough# by Restday.

rule @frost_bark
when concept=bark here.time=dawn here.season=winter self.likes=frosty_mornings
does aside
cooldown 12h
say #whitefrost.capitalize#. Good. | There it is. Frost on the railings.

rule @song_bark
when concept=bark here.time=dusk self.likes=singing
does aside
cooldown 12h
say Mm. The low part goes here. | #song.capitalize#, and then supper.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. Sit down, do. What is it? | #greet#. Take your time. What's wanted?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #greet#, #topic.player#. You look well. What can I do?
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : It's late. If someone's ill, tell me where. If not, it'll keep till morning.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : #greet#. Say what you need. I'll listen.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=healer] : I'm a physician. I visit the sick on the hill, with #bag# and whatever I've mixed myself. | I sit with sick folk and help them mend. Mostly I listen.
dlg @2 resident.job : I work. Slowly, and carefully. | #job_busy#
dlg @1 resident.business [business=thriving] : #hill.capitalize# keeps me busy. More than I'd wish on it. | Busy. Too busy, for the patients' sake.
dlg @2 resident.business [business=failing] : Few calls, and fewer who can pay. I go anyway.
dlg @3 resident.business [business!=thriving|failing] : Steady. Nobody worse today than yesterday. | #fine#. That's all a physician can ask.
dlg @1 resident.news [!world.news !world.event_words world.wagons!=raided world.death!=recent world.wedding!=recent] : #news_none# The sick don't talk of much besides their own aches. | Nothing that I know of.
dlg @2 resident.news [world.news] : I heard from #world.news_from#: #world.news#. #patient.capitalize# told me.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip!=yes] : #gossip_none# | Nothing leaves a sick room. Not from me.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. Go gently. | #farewell#. Keep warm.
graft resident.hub
choice Why won't you use a House's remedies? [self.job=healer] -> physic
node physic
say Because I don't know who stood at their still, or what they wanted from it. I mix every remedy myself. Then I know what I'm giving.
mood calm
free
choice Is that not a lot of work? -> physic_work
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node physic_work
say It is. It's slow. But slow is #remedy# too. Nobody's been worse for waiting an hour for something I trust.
choice I see. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
